config DRM_PVR_MTK_DDK
	tristate "MediaTek PowerVR Rogue DDK 1.13 (pvrsrvkm) for MT6765"
	depends on DRM && ARM64 && OF
	depends on COMMON_CLK && PM
	select DMA_SHARED_BUFFER
	select SYNC_FILE
	select FW_LOADER
	help
	  Port of the Imagination PowerVR Rogue services kernel driver
	  shipped by MediaTek in the stock Rabbit R1 kernel
	  (DDK 1.13, m1.13ED5776728, GE8320 BVNC 22.87.104.18).

	  The userspace bridge ABI (ioctls, bridge tables and the "pvr"
	  DRM driver) is kept identical to the stock DDK so that the
	  stock Android userspace GPU blobs can talk to it. This is not
	  the upstream "powervr" DRM driver and does not share its UAPI.

	  The module is called pvrsrvkm and loads the firmware files
	  rgx.fw and rgx.sh.
